    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d551">

                <pb facs="0915" n="779" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg779"/>

                <head>No. 551.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Sir L. S. Sackville West to Mr.
                        Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-02-05"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 5, 1888</date>.
                        (Received February 7.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the case of certain
                    American vessels in distress at Halifax I have the honor to inform you that the
                    Marquis of <pb facs="0916" n="780" xml:id="pg780"/> Salisbury has telegraphed to
                    me to the effect that permission has been granted to land part of their
                    perishable cargo in order to operate <hi rendition="#italic">bona fide</hi>
                    repairs, but without prejudice to the question of right.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">L. S. Sackville
                    West.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
